  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Lexicon and Plate",
    "overview": "Backwater Trace is set as a reference book about Alappuzha's incidents. Each incident is an entry with a serif headword, its source reports are numbered citations, and a disagreement between sources is a variant reading, marked in vermilion and engraver's cross-hatch. The page is engraving black on uncoated stock paper, divided by hairlines and 3px double rules, with square corners everywhere a reader's eye lands. Colour does not wash across the page. It lives inside bordered plates: the map, product screens reproduced on the landing page, and the small category ink squares.\n\nDensity follows a working reference book rather than a dashboard. The board is three ruled columns (entry list, map plate, record column) under a double-ruled masthead. The landing page is a book spread: a shoulder index of incident kinds, a display headline over a double rule with a drawn fleuron, and numbered plates with captions and keyed callouts. Instrument Serif carries every head, entry title and guide word at weight 400 only; Geist carries the working text; Chilanka is a first-class face, not a fallback.\n\nThe signature move is the dashboard's live guide words. As in a printed dictionary, the head of the entry list shows the first and last entry in view, and they are recomputed on every scroll frame. The logo is the drop-and-canal mark from `docs/brand/final/`, used as supplied.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Engraving black (#1a1712) on stock paper (#f7f3ea); no dark theme.",
      "Hairline rules for division, 3px double rules for frames and section heads.",
      "Square corners; the only circles are map pins and source dots.",
      "Colour only inside bordered plates and category ink squares.",
      "Ultramarine is the single action colour; vermilion plus 90-degree cross-hatch means possible conflict only.",
      "Instrument Serif at weight 400 for heads, entries and guide words; Geist for working text; tabular figures for readings.",
      "Live guide words at the head of the entry list."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Plate Rule",
        "body": "Colour is printed only inside a frame: the map plate, a reproduced screen, a category ink square. The page itself stays black on stock.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Action Rule",
        "body": "Ultramarine marks what can be done. Nothing decorative is ultramarine; the Flood ink is a category, not an action.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Variant Reading Rule",
        "body": "Vermilion appears only with cross-hatch, and only for a possible conflict between sources. Errors use Danger (#8f1d1d), never vermilion.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Faux Bold Rule",
        "body": "Instrument Serif is set at weight 400 only, with `font-synthesis: none`. Emphasis in the serif comes from size or italic, never weight.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Part of Speech Rule",
        "body": "A category name is set italic, lowercase, in the serif, directly after its ink square, as a dictionary marks a word class.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Reading Rule",
        "body": "Any figure a coordinator compares (counts, times, sources, citation numbers) uses tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraved Frame Rule",
        "body": "Where another system would raise a card, this one draws a second rule around it. No surface uses a drop shadow to claim importance.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every head, entry title and guide word in Instrument Serif at weight 400.",
      "Do frame colour: put map, screenshots and category inks inside a 1px black border with an offset second rule.",
      "Do close sheets, mastheads and major sections with a 3px double rule (`border-bottom: 3px double`), and divide items with 1px hairlines (#d6cdba).",
      "Do give every button the inner double-rule frame, and keep ultramarine for actions only.",
      "Do pair vermilion with the 90-degree cross-hatch every time it appears.",
      "Do write category names italic and lowercase after their ink square.",
      "Do use tabular figures for counts, times and source totals.",
      "Do use the logo masters from `docs/brand/final/` exactly as supplied, on a solid container."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't bold, synthesize or uppercase-track Instrument Serif.",
      "Don't round corners; circles are reserved for map pins and source dots.",
      "Don't lift surfaces with drop shadows; draw a rule instead.",
      "Don't use vermilion for errors, emphasis or decoration; errors use Danger (#8f1d1d).",
      "Don't flood a page or panel with a category ink or ultramarine background.",
      "Don't recolour, redraw or retype the logo.",
      "Don't add a dark theme; the world is printed stock."
